.TH SPACEGL_SERVER 1 "2026-04-19" "SpaceGL @VERSION@" "SpaceGL Manual"
.SH NAME
spacegl_server \- SpaceGL galaxy server daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spacegl_server
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spacegl_server
is the central game server for the SpaceGL multi-user 3D space engine.
It manages galaxy state, player sessions, NPC entities, and secure
communication channels via shared memory (SHM) and TCP networking on
port 5000.
.PP
Authentication is performed through a master key provided via the
.B SPACEGL_KEY
environment variable or interactively at startup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d
Enable debug mode (verbose logging).
.TP
.B \-\-data-dir DIR
Root directory for the server's persistent state: the
.IR captains/ \(em captain profiles, identity records and frequency
keys \(em and the
.I galaxy.dat
file are stored under this directory instead of the current working
directory (the default, kept for backward compatibility). The directory
is created at startup if it does not exist. Note: pointing the server at
a directory without an existing
galaxy.dat
starts a fresh galaxy.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SPACEGL_KEY
Master authentication key for the server session.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/spacegl_server
Server executable.
.TP
.I [DATA\-DIR]/galaxy.dat
Serialized galaxy state (default: ./galaxy.dat).
.TP
.I [DATA\-DIR]/captains/
captain profiles, identity records and frequency keys
(default: ./captains/).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR spacegl_client (1),
.BR spacegl-server (1),
.BR spacegl_3dview (1),
.BR spacegl_vulkan (1)
